Reproduced offline (bug hunt 2026-09-26).

1) lib/Langertha/CachedContent.pm:253-263 to_create_body "peels" Tool->format_list("gemini") down to its functionDeclarations array and sends that as body.tools. The cachedContents REST field is tools: Tool[] where each Tool is { functionDeclarations: [...] } (same shape as generateContent tools). Result on the wire: tools:[{"name":"f","description":"d","parameters":{...}}] -> expected 400 (unknown field name in Tool). Fix: send format_list output unpeeled.
   Repro: Langertha::CachedContent->new(model=>"models/gemini-2.5-pro", ttl=>"60s", tools=>[{name=>"f",description=>"d",input_schema=>{type=>"object",properties=>{}}}])->to_create_body->{tools}

2) lib/Langertha/CachedContent.pm:320 from_hash reads $hash->{expiration}{ttl|expireTime}. expiration is a proto oneof; proto3 JSON flattens it, so real GET/POST/LIST responses carry top-level "expireTime" (ttl is input-only). expire_time is therefore never set on a parsed server resource and is_expired (:384) falls back to ttl, which is also absent -> always 0.
   Repro: Langertha::CachedContent->from_hash({name=>"cachedContents/x", model=>"m", expireTime=>"2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"}) -> expire_time undef, is_expired 0.
   Fix: read top-level expireTime/ttl (keep the wrapper as a tolerated alternate spelling, ADR 0018). The t/47_gemini_cached_content.t payloads are hand-written with the wrapper (karr #92 pattern); replace with a doc-sourced or captured shape.

3) (provider-reality, needs langertha-llm-advisor to confirm) lib/Langertha/Engine/Gemini.pm:332/345 and :680/691: with a bound cached_content, chat_request still sends systemInstruction (from the engine system_prompt), tools and toolConfig. Gemini documents that a generateContent request referencing cachedContent may not also set system_instruction, tools or tool_config (400 "CachedContent can not be used with GenerateContent request setting system_instruction, tools or tool_config"). Suggested: croak/carp early or drop them with a carp when cached_content is bound.
